Project-authored code and documentation: Apache License, Version 2.0.

The following parts are adapted to this project's interfaces and C11
(assembly where applicable). Each file names all contributing Asteria
source files in its Origin comment:

- Host timing and interrupt guards: host/amd64/calibration.c, time.c, hal.c.
- Host interrupt routing and IOMMU handoff:
  host/amd64/intx.c, iommu_tables.c; tests in
  host/amd64/tests/prep.c.
- USB xHCI/EHCI/BOT/SCSI and AHCI persistence: host/amd64/plog_xhci.c,
  plog_ehci.c, plog_ahci.c, persist/bot.c, persist/protocol.c, persist/sbc.c.
- AML parsing, opcode grammar and routing facts: platform/aml.c, aml.h,
  aml-grammar.h, acpi-irq.c; tests in platform/tests/aml.c and aml-core.asl.
- PCI addressing, BAR probing, MSI, INTx, IOSAPIC, PIB and locking:
  platform/pci.c, msi.c, intx.c, iosapic.c, pib.c, lock.h;
  tests in tests/hosted/platform.c.
- UART probe tests: tests/loaders/physical.c.
- Firmware timer, IVT, translation activation, PCI ECAM and SAL tables:
  firmware/new/dxe/arch.c, ivt.S, gate/virtual.S, boot-translation.h,
  pci/root.c, sal/sal.c, sal/table.c; tests in
  tests/firmware/sal.c.
- EFI linker layout and ELF-to-PE conversion: firmware/edk2/module.lds,
  tools/firmware/elf_to_pe.py, tests/firmware/test_converter.py.

Asteria's third-party font and cryptographic test data are not included in
these ports. Its project-code notice above is retained; the licence is
